{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundled UI chooses a platform-appropriate default while exposing the iOS presentation style. The same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.dismiss)"},{"type":"text","text":" action fires from every presentation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This article explains the reasoning behind those choices and what is fixed versus configurable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"revenueCatPaywall","text":"revenueCatPaywall","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Platform"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Presentation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reason"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS, compact width"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fullScreenCover"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compact screens keep the paywall immersive and avoid a cramped sheet."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS, regular width"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iPad and other regular-width hosts follow RevenueCatUI’s sheet default."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"frame(minWidth: 400, minHeight: 600)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mac sheets do not expand to fill the parent window. Without an explicit minimum size the paywall would render too small to legibly show plan options. The 400×600 minimum is roughly the size RevenueCatUI’s templates assume."}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".automatic"},{"type":"text","text":" style uses the table above. iOS callers can force "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fullScreen"},{"type":"text","text":"; macOS always uses a sheet. The modifiers show "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s close button by default. When the close button is disabled, iOS sheets also disable interactive dismissal. On macOS, Escape clears the presentation binding only when the close button is enabled. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"displayCloseButton: false"},{"type":"text","text":" only for a hard paywall the user must purchase through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The minimum frame is hard-coded; it is not exposed as a parameter. If your paywall layout needs more room on macOS, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI.PaywallView"},{"type":"text","text":" directly inside a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"revenueCatCustomerCenter","text":"revenueCatCustomerCenter","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Platform"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Presentation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reason"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI.CustomerCenterView"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCatUI ships a customer center on iOS only. A non-fullscreen "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sheet"},{"type":"text","text":" is appropriate because customer-center actions are administrative, not part of a purchase flow."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opens "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":", then clears the request"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCatUI does not ship a customer center on macOS, and the system has no equivalent in-app surface. The primitive modifier uses SwiftUI’s URL opener and fires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDismiss"},{"type":"text","text":"; the composed modifier dispatches the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".openManageSubscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" actions."}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With the composed modifier, the macOS branch dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".openManageSubscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", then clears the binding to dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":". The plugin’s URL opener is injectable, so apps and tests can control the external hand-off. The primitive binding-based modifier uses SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" environment action and falls back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" when nothing handles the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps"},{"type":"text","text":" scheme."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Presentation-coordination","text":"Presentation coordination","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS, the composed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revenueCatPaywallAndCustomerCenter(state:offeringIdentifier:displayCloseButton:fonts:presentationStyle:purchaseLogic:onEvent:onAction:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier never shows the paywall and customer center at once. The paywall wins: while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.isPresented"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", the customer-center binding reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and an initial or later state with both flags set dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS, subscription management is an external App Store hand-off rather than a second modal surface. The customer-center binding remains active while the paywall sheet is open, so the composed modifier dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".openManageSubscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" without losing the request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps wiring the primitive modifiers manually own the iOS exclusivity rule."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"One-app-wide-attachment","text":"One app-wide attachment","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach the composed modifier once, to one app-wide presentation host. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"type":"text","text":" is shared, so attaching the modifier inside every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" window or scene makes every copy respond to the same request. A multi-window app should choose one scene, such as its primary app or settings window, to own paywall presentation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Exit-offers","text":"Exit offers","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCat dashboard exit offers are unavailable through the bundled modifiers. RevenueCatUI implements exit offers in its own presentation modifiers, which always add a close button. This package embeds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallView"},{"type":"text","text":" so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"displayCloseButton: false"},{"type":"text","text":" remains a hard paywall. Use RevenueCatUI’s presenter directly when exit offers are required."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-is-configurable","text":"What is configurable","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The configurable surface lives in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI"},{"type":"text","text":" and on the paywall plugin:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Paywall content, copy, and template","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — configured in the RevenueCat dashboard. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI.PaywallView"},{"type":"text","text":" renders whichever offering and template the dashboard returns."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Customer-center labels, sections, and actions","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — configured in the RevenueCat dashboard. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatUI.CustomerCenterView"},{"type":"text","text":" renders whichever configuration the dashboard returns."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Close button","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"displayCloseButton:"},{"type":"text","text":" on the paywall modifiers. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"; pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" for a hard paywall."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fonts","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fonts:"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts any RevenueCatUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallFontProvider"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Presentation","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presentationStyle:"},{"type":"text","text":" controls iOS sheet or full-screen presentation; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".automatic"},{"type":"text","text":" follows horizontal size class."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Outcomes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onEvent:"},{"type":"text","text":" reports package-owned purchase, restore, cancellation, and failure values from inside the presentation boundary."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Presentation triggering","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — driven by the plugin via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.isPresented"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCustomerCenterPresented"},{"type":"text","text":". Your code chooses "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"when","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to set them via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".presentCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" actions."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dismiss behavior","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — dismiss actions are dispatched by the presentation bindings themselves ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismiss"},{"type":"text","text":" for the paywall, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dismissCustomerCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" for the customer center). The primitive modifiers’ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDismiss"},{"type":"text","text":" callbacks are purely additive — use them for analytics hooks or cleanup, not for dispatch."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Offering selection","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"offeringIdentifier:"},{"type":"text","text":" presents a specific offering and takes precedence over placement targeting. The composed modifier otherwise passes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState.requestedReason"},{"type":"text","text":" as a RevenueCat placement. For an unknown placement, RevenueCat may return the dashboard’s placement fallback offering, which can differ from the current offering; the package uses the current offering when RevenueCat returns no placement fallback or the fetch fails. An unknown explicit identifier also asserts in Debug and logs a warning."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/PlatformBehavior"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" documentation provides the matching API reference for the modifiers described here.","type":"text"}],"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPresentTheUI"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping"],"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"How the paywall and customer-center modifiers choose presentation, and which controls remain fixed.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/platformbehavior"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Platform Behavior","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/HowToPresentTheUI":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPresentTheUI","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/howtopresenttheui","type":"topic","title":"How to Present the UI","abstract":[{"text":"Attach ","type":"text"},{"code":"revenueCatPaywallAndCustomerCenter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to a root view to present both surfaces from ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or attach either binding-driven primitive by itself.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall","type":"topic","title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCat adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Implements "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", ships a controllable mock for previews and tests, and pairs with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" for drop-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallView"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerCenterView"},{"type":"text","text":" presentation."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/EntitlementMapping":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/entitlementmapping","type":"topic","title":"Entitlement Mapping","abstract":[{"text":"How RevenueCat’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomerInfo.entitlements","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" translates to Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article"}}}